{"authored" [{"question" "q-163812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solution curves of the differential equation ${y}^{2}{y}^{′}=y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Which of the following are stationary points of their respective solution curve?\n\n- $(\\pi ,1)$\n- $(\\pi ,-1)$\n- $(0,-1)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-163812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stationary point of $y(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $y$ such that ${y}^{′}(c)=0.$ \n\nFirst, we make ${y}^{′}$ the subject of the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}{y}^{′}=y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,⟹\\,{y}^{′}=\\frac{y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of our points into the differential equation and calculate the value of the derivative: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{y}^{′}|}_{(\\pi ,1)} & ={(\\frac{y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{y}^{2}})|}_{(\\pi ,1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =0\\,✓ \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(\\pi ,-1)} & ={(\\frac{y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{y}^{2}})|}_{(\\pi ,-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =-2 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(0,-1)} & ={(\\frac{y+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{{y}^{2}})|}_{(0,-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)}{(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =0\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-163812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "234e455c2dee377dfe715b4cdab3567ed786226ac9b4cba358209b69c859b258" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-163812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-163812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-163812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"ques