a256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89871" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "None of the points are the stationary points of the function"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the solution curves of the differential equation ${y}^{′}-y={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}.$ Which of the following are stationary points of their respective solution curve?\n\n- $(-1,-2)$\n- $(1,1)$\n- $(1,-2)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a stationary point of $y(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $y$ such that ${y}^{′}(c)=0.$ \n\nFirst, we make ${y}^{′}$ the subject of the equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-y={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{′}={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of our points into the differential equation and calculate the value of the derivative: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{y}^{′}|}_{(-1,-2)} & ={({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+y)|}_{(-1,-2)} \\\\  & =(-1)^{3}+3(-1)^{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =0\\,✓ \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(1,1)} & ={({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+y)|}_{(1,1)} \\\\  & =(1)^{3}+3(1)^{2}+(1) \\\\  & =5 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ {{y}^{′}|}_{(1,-2)} & ={({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+y)|}_{(1,-2)} \\\\  & =(1)^{3}+3(1)^{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =2 \\\\  & \\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89414" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "234e455c2dee377dfe715b4cdab3567ed786226ac9b4cba358209b69c859b258" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-89414" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14035334/state.json" "file_sha256" "f3ff58676550e44dc400467358c6732bfddd8dcce979c9bcfdd8240e507c99ce" "basis" 1240 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1403533